        <extension url="http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/valueset-rules-text">
          <valueMarkdown value="https://mor.nlm.nih.gov/RxMix/ Script: &#xD;&#xA;Step 1 Upload to RxMix a workflow config file  named GetRelatedByType.config containing the following workflow text: &lt;WFE&gt;&lt;filteredOutputs&gt;RXCUI|name|term_type&lt;/filteredOutputs&gt;&lt;input&gt;NOINPUT&lt;/input&gt;&lt;FS&gt;&lt;service&gt;NOINPUT&lt;/service&gt;&lt;function&gt;getRelatedByType&lt;/function&gt;&lt;level&gt;0&lt;/level&gt;&lt;paramSize&gt;2&lt;/paramSize&gt;&lt;param order ='0'&gt;?&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param order ='1'&gt;BPCK,GPCK,SBD,SCD&lt;/param&gt;&lt;/FS&gt;&lt;/WFE&gt; &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Step 2 Create Batch text input file (Ingredients.txt) with following RxNorm Fentanyl-type ingredient codes representing fentanyl, sufentanil, alfentanil, remifentanil as an input within the file:&#xD;&#xA;4337&#xD;&#xA;56795&#xD;&#xA;480&#xD;&#xA;73032&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Step 3 Upload the batch text input file Ingredients.txt created in step 2. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Step 4 Submit the batch which will run the workflow using the input codes to generate a combined set of all the concepts needed..&#xD;&#xA;"/>
        </extension>
